    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components",
    "problem": "Find the angle between $a=⟨4,-3,2⟩$ and $b=⟨3,4,1⟩.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
    "worked_solution": "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{29}\\cdot \\sqrt{26}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{754}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{754}})≈{85.82}^{∘}.\n$$",
